Title: The Last Lantern — Performance Pilot

INT. WATCHTOWER - NIGHT

BED: Quiet wind outside a stone watchtower, no voices, subdued continuous ambience.

MIRA
(Whisper the whole line, breathy rather than ordinary quiet speech; exhausted and urgently hoping to hear an answer, slow carefully over the last word.)
[whispers] Are you still there?

NARRATOR
(Begin close and restrained; let the silence hang before describing her tightening grip.)
Mira whispered, gripping the lantern. She had waited all night for an answer. Then the bell began to shake above her.

SFX: A single brief iron bell strike, resonant but restrained.

MIRA
(Shout the whole outburst, with projected urgent effort rather than normal conversation; build force and alarm toward the final word.)
Get away from the door!

NARRATOR
(Catch the sudden outburst, then settle into the uneasy stillness that follows.)
Her shout filled the tower. Outside, the footsteps stopped.
